BHĪ, Ⅰ. Ā. bháya, (ord. form in V.), 🞄Ⅲ. P. bibhé-ti, fear, be afraid of (ab., 🞄g.);
 be anxious about (ab.): mā bhaiḥ or 🞄bhaiṣīḥ, fear not: pp. bhītá, frightened, 🞄alarmed, dreading, afraid of (ab., g., —˚);
 imperilled;
 🞄anxious about (—˚);
 cs. bhīṣáya, 🞄P. Ā., bhāyaya, P. frighten, terrify, intimidate. 🞄ati, be excessively afraid. pra, be 🞄frightened of (ab.): pp. terrified. vi, be 🞄frightened: pp. frightened;
 cs. frighten, intimidate. 🞄sam, pp. dreading (g.).
